-- title:
--   Crossing chart from a crossing presentation of a stalk
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, $\varpi \in O$ and $e \in \mathbb{N}$, and write $C = \mathrm{CrossingQuotient}\,O\,(\varpi^e)$ for the quotient of the polynomial ring $O[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi^e$; assume $C$ is a domain and is integrally closed. Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme, $\pi_X \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} O$ a morphism locally of finite type, and $x \in X$ a point whose singleton is closed. Write $\bar{\varpi} \in \Gamma(X,\top)$ for the image of $\varpi$ under $\pi_X$ on global sections. Suppose given $g, h$ in the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ with: $gh$ equal to the $e$-th power of the germ of $\bar{\varpi}$ at $x$; the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ equal to the ideal generated by that germ together with $g$ and $h$; the map sending $o \in O$ to the residue class of the germ of its image in $\Gamma(X,\top)$ surjective onto the residue field of $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$; and $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} C \le \operatorname{ringKrullDim} \mathcal{O}_{X,x}$. Then there are an open $U \ni x$, sections $g_U, h_U \in \Gamma(X,U)$ and a morphism $f \colon U \to \operatorname{Spec} C$ such that the germs of $g_U, h_U$ at $x$ are $g, h$; $g_U h_U$ equals the $e$-th power of the restriction of $\bar{\varpi}$ to $U$; $f$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $O \to C$ equals the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow X$ followed by $\pi_X$; for $y \in U$, the prime $f(y)$ contains both of the designated elements $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient.U}\,(\varpi^e)$ and $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient.V}\,(\varpi^e)$ of $C$ if and only if $y$ maps to $x$; for every $y$ lying over $x$ the induced map of stalks is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal, and induces an isomorphism of residue fields; and for $y \in U$, the prime $f(y)$ contains $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient.U}\,(\varpi^e)$ exactly when $y$ lies outside the basic open set of $g_U$, and contains $\mathrm{CrossingQuotient.V}\,(\varpi^e)$ exactly when $y$ lies outside the basic open set of $h_U$. Thus the local conclusion at points over $x$ is flatness together with the unramifiedness data (maximal ideal generated, residue field isomorphism), not an assertion of étaleness as such.
--
--   This is the scheme-theoretic local structure statement at an ordinary double point of a relative curve: a crossing presentation $gh = \varpi^e$, $\mathfrak{m}_x = (\varpi, g, h)$ of the local ring, with $O$ surjecting onto $\kappa(x)$, is spread out to a chart over $\operatorname{Spec} O[u,v]/(uv-\varpi^e)$ whose vertex fibre over $x$ is a single point. It is used in the construction of oriented crossing charts on Deligne–Rapoport models of modular curves, and its local flatness and unramifiedness are obtained from the criterion [`Algebra.IsUnramifiedAt.isEtaleAt_of_ringKrullDim_le`](thm.html#Algebra.IsUnramifiedAt.isEtaleAt_of_ringKrullDim_le).
